==English==

{{slim-wikipedia|dab=Stair}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|staire|lang=enm}}, {{term|stayre|lang=enm}}, {{term|stayer|lang=enm}}, {{term|steir|lang=enm}}, {{term|steyre|lang=enm}}, {{term|steyer|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|stǣġer||stair, staircase}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*staigriz||stairs, scaffolding}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*steygʰ-||to walk, proceed, march, climb}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|steiger||a stair, step, wharf, pier, scaffolding|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|steiger|lang=gml}}, {{term|steir||scaffolding|lang=gml}}. Related to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|āstǣgan||to ascend, go up, embark}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|stīgan||to go, move, reach; ascend, mount, go up, spring up, rise; scale}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Stiege||a flight of stairs|lang=de}}. More at {{l|en|sty}}.

